# Toolchain and CI

- `go.mod` sets the minimum Go version; CI derives the Go minor version from its `go` line and installs the latest patch of that minor. `ignore ./frontend/node_modules` keeps npm-shipped Go packages out of `./...`.
- `.github/workflows/ci.yml` runs the frontend job (`npm ci`, `npm run lint`, `npm test`, `npm run build`), the shell job (`shellcheck scripts/*.sh`; write `CDPATH=''`, not `CDPATH=`, SC1007) and then the Go job with the built `frontend/dist` artifact: the generated-types freshness check (`scripts/gen-types.sh` + `git diff --exit-code`), the hidden-character check, `go vet`, `staticcheck`, `govulncheck`, `go test -race`. It is also a reusable workflow (`workflow_call`) for the release. Keep local verification aligned with it.
- `.github/workflows/release.yml` runs on a pushed `v*` tag: tag format and changelog notes, then `ci.yml`, then `scripts/release.sh` (no dependency caches) with an `actions/attest` build provenance attestation, then `gh release create` (prerelease when the tag has a `-`). Workflow permissions are `{}`; each job asks for its own. Use current major versions of actions (look them up) and keep `ci.yml` and `release.yml` on the same ones.
- `scripts/release.sh [--skip-web] VERSION [OUTDIR]` (default `dist/release`, ignored by git) builds the release files whose names `docs/RELEASING.md` and the installer rely on: reproducible archives (GNU tar, sorted members with explicit modes, owner 0, `SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH` or commit time, `gzip -n`), `install.sh` with `RELEASE_VERSION` stamped, `SHA256SUMS` in plain `sha256sum` form. It must keep working on Linux and in Git Bash on Windows (no reliance on file modes; GNU tar reads `C:`-style paths as remote hosts, so use `/c/...` paths or `--force-local`). `scripts/release-notes.sh VERSION` prints the version's `CHANGELOG.md` section (Keep a Changelog `## [X.Y.Z] - DATE`) and fails when it is missing.
- ESLint uses the flat config in `frontend/eslint.config.js` (`typescript-eslint`, `eslint-plugin-react-hooks`) with `--max-warnings=0`. Disable a rule only on the specific line, with a comment explaining why.
- `frontend/package-lock.json` must stay `npm ci`-compatible; commit it with dependency changes.
- Vite empties `frontend/dist` on build; the `keep-dist-placeholder` plugin in `vite.config.ts` restores the committed `.gitkeep`.
- `scripts/build.sh` builds the web client then `bin/golem-deploy` (extra arguments go to `go build`, e.g. `-ldflags "-X main.version=..."`). `scripts/gen-types.sh` regenerates `frontend/src/api/types.gen.ts` with tygo at the version pinned in the script; bump it there only.
- Text files use LF line endings (`.gitattributes`). `go run ./scripts/checkchars` (CI and locally, any OS) fails on bidi controls (U+202A–U+202E, U+2066–U+2069, U+200E/U+200F, U+061C), U+2028/U+2029, NUL and other C0 controls except tab/LF/CR in tracked files (binary extensions skipped). Write such characters as escapes in tests; its `allowlist` (with a reason per file) stays empty unless a fixture truly needs them.
